WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.260
This module is going to cover what content actually works.

2
00:00:03.260 --> 00:00:05.160
We're going to talk about hooks, consistency,

3
00:00:05.160 --> 00:00:08.160
collecting emails, and how much to post to build momentum.

4
00:00:08.160 --> 00:00:10.920
So now that you know why content works and where to post,

5
00:00:10.920 --> 00:00:12.680
that's now talk about what actually works

6
00:00:12.680 --> 00:00:13.880
and how much you need to do.

7
00:00:13.880 --> 00:00:16.880
And if you were to master just one thing in the content game,

8
00:00:16.880 --> 00:00:19.040
I would say it has to be hooks.

9
00:00:19.040 --> 00:00:20.160
And a hook is very simple.

10
00:00:20.160 --> 00:00:23.000
It's the very first sentence, the very first intro,

11
00:00:23.000 --> 00:00:26.600
the very first visual that you say and show in the video,

12
00:00:26.600 --> 00:00:29.320
because that's what the algorithm really cares about.

13
00:00:29.320 --> 00:00:31.240
And the reason why the algorithm cares about it

14
00:00:31.240 --> 00:00:33.800
is because a strong hook keeps people watching.

15
00:00:33.800 --> 00:00:35.440
And so you just need to practice this.

16
00:00:35.440 --> 00:00:36.600
Now, especially when you're beginning,

17
00:00:36.600 --> 00:00:40.360
I'd say don't worry so much about polish and production quality.

18
00:00:40.360 --> 00:00:42.000
And just to give you a concrete example,

19
00:00:42.000 --> 00:00:44.040
if you go to some of our most viral videos

20
00:00:44.040 --> 00:00:47.240
here at RoboNuggets, you can notice how I use the hooks

21
00:00:47.240 --> 00:00:49.240
in order to actually get people to watch.

22
00:00:49.240 --> 00:00:52.000
So if I just open this, one technique that I like to use

23
00:00:52.000 --> 00:00:54.120
is to have some sort of headline in there.

24
00:00:54.120 --> 00:00:55.840
And that headline needs to be interesting,

25
00:00:55.840 --> 00:00:56.840
it needs to be arresting.

26
00:00:56.840 --> 00:00:59.080
And during this time, this was 2024,

27
00:00:59.080 --> 00:01:01.560
I found this prompt that was going viral on Reddit,

28
00:01:01.560 --> 00:01:03.000
which was basically this one.

29
00:01:03.000 --> 00:01:04.560
And this prompt that I posted in this long one

30
00:01:04.560 --> 00:01:06.880
by this Reddit user, whom I attribute it as well.

31
00:01:06.880 --> 00:01:08.360
But I just found, when I tried it,

32
00:01:08.360 --> 00:01:09.880
that it was actually quite revealing.

33
00:01:09.880 --> 00:01:10.920
And during this time,

34
00:01:10.920 --> 00:01:13.880
prompts that are really powerful were not as prevalent yet.

35
00:01:13.880 --> 00:01:16.640
And so I just did a quick video sharing my experience.

36
00:01:16.640 --> 00:01:18.000
But what I wanted you to notice

37
00:01:18.000 --> 00:01:20.680
is instead of just saying that I found a really good prompt,

38
00:01:20.680 --> 00:01:23.760
or instead of just repeating the title of this thread,

39
00:01:23.760 --> 00:01:27.400
what I did here is branded as the God prompt for chat GPT.

40
00:01:27.400 --> 00:01:29.440
And so that just gives you a bit of curiosity

41
00:01:29.440 --> 00:01:31.000
on what exactly is the God prompt,

42
00:01:31.000 --> 00:01:32.720
and is it something that I can use?

43
00:01:32.720 --> 00:01:33.720
And if I play this,

44
00:01:33.720 --> 00:01:36.560
did I just find the God prompt for chat GPT?

45
00:01:36.560 --> 00:01:37.640
So I was rousing Reddit,

46
00:01:37.640 --> 00:01:39.720
and I came across this thread that asked,

47
00:01:39.720 --> 00:01:41.200
that was literally the hook, right?

48
00:01:41.200 --> 00:01:42.840
So I packaged it and called it something

49
00:01:42.840 --> 00:01:44.720
that people I think would find interesting.

50
00:01:44.720 --> 00:01:46.120
And also, if you notice,

51
00:01:46.120 --> 00:01:48.240
the reason why I use this orange on a stick

52
00:01:48.240 --> 00:01:50.400
is because one of the hooks that you can introduce

53
00:01:50.400 --> 00:01:52.280
is also have a visual hook.

54
00:01:52.280 --> 00:01:53.520
So apart from the verbal hook,

55
00:01:53.520 --> 00:01:54.800
which is the packaging here,

56
00:01:54.800 --> 00:01:56.200
and having this headline title

57
00:01:56.200 --> 00:01:57.720
that people can just easily read,

58
00:01:57.720 --> 00:01:59.360
a lot of people in a lot of comments,

59
00:01:59.360 --> 00:02:01.840
most especially, also talk about this orange,

60
00:02:01.840 --> 00:02:03.480
and because they're curious about what it is

61
00:02:03.480 --> 00:02:05.360
and what pointer I'm specifically using,

62
00:02:05.360 --> 00:02:06.600
that actually gets them to comment,

63
00:02:06.600 --> 00:02:07.800
that actually gets them to watch,

64
00:02:07.800 --> 00:02:10.120
and that curiosity gap, as they call it,

65
00:02:10.120 --> 00:02:11.640
is so strong, I guess,

66
00:02:11.640 --> 00:02:13.440
that people watched it till the end,

67
00:02:13.440 --> 00:02:15.640
and this got 4.6 million views.

68
00:02:15.640 --> 00:02:17.240
Now hooks will get you really far,

69
00:02:17.240 --> 00:02:19.520
and they always say that a video with a really good hook,

70
00:02:19.520 --> 00:02:21.320
but where the content is quite poor,

71
00:02:21.320 --> 00:02:23.880
will still outperform a specific video

72
00:02:23.880 --> 00:02:25.200
where the content was really great,

73
00:02:25.200 --> 00:02:27.320
but the hook in the beginning is not that great.

74
00:02:27.320 --> 00:02:29.280
That's why, interestingly, in the world of content,

75
00:02:29.280 --> 00:02:32.040
hooks are always going to be the top thing

76
00:02:32.040 --> 00:02:34.080
that you should master instead of the content itself.

77
00:02:34.080 --> 00:02:36.320
Now that is not to say that hooks alone

78
00:02:36.320 --> 00:02:37.520
will get you to success.

79
00:02:37.520 --> 00:02:38.720
It can get you very far,

80
00:02:38.720 --> 00:02:39.560
but if you notice,

81
00:02:39.560 --> 00:02:42.040
the part of the reason why this got viral as well

82
00:02:42.040 --> 00:02:44.080
is because the actual prompt that was shared

83
00:02:44.080 --> 00:02:45.640
is actually really useful.

84
00:02:45.640 --> 00:02:46.960
And so even though I'd say that the hook

85
00:02:46.960 --> 00:02:48.840
is more important than the content itself,

86
00:02:48.840 --> 00:02:50.920
for most cases, what you should always aim for

87
00:02:50.920 --> 00:02:53.000
is to have that sort of great combination

88
00:02:53.000 --> 00:02:55.920
of a great hook and obviously great content still,

89
00:02:55.920 --> 00:02:57.480
because that's what people are watching for

90
00:02:57.480 --> 00:03:00.080
and what people will follow you for over time.

91
00:03:00.080 --> 00:03:02.560
Now the second strategy that I would impart to you

92
00:03:02.560 --> 00:03:03.840
is all about consistency.

93
00:03:03.840 --> 00:03:05.280
So especially when you're just beginning,

94
00:03:05.280 --> 00:03:07.680
my advice to you is don't worry about polish

95
00:03:07.680 --> 00:03:10.320
or high quality cameras in the beginning yet.

96
00:03:10.320 --> 00:03:12.120
You should just focus on publishing

97
00:03:12.120 --> 00:03:14.320
and talking about AI as much as possible

98
00:03:14.320 --> 00:03:15.400
in a given day or week.

99
00:03:15.400 --> 00:03:17.600
And even though it appears like everyone is talking

100
00:03:17.600 --> 00:03:19.880
about AI that the space looks crowded,

101
00:03:19.880 --> 00:03:22.280
remember that your specific situation

102
00:03:22.280 --> 00:03:25.440
and your specific context will always be unique.

103
00:03:25.440 --> 00:03:27.520
So maybe you can talk about AI for real estate

104
00:03:27.520 --> 00:03:29.520
or you can talk about AI for creatives

105
00:03:29.520 --> 00:03:33.000
or you can talk about AI for fitness influencers, for example.

106
00:03:33.000 --> 00:03:36.080
There will always be a specific combination of insights

107
00:03:36.080 --> 00:03:37.960
that only you can bring to the table.

108
00:03:37.960 --> 00:03:40.520
And so my advice to you is to focus on publishing

109
00:03:40.520 --> 00:03:42.080
as much as possible, focus on shipping

110
00:03:42.080 --> 00:03:43.360
in a given day or week

111
00:03:43.360 --> 00:03:45.640
and then just improve 1% every time.

112
00:03:45.640 --> 00:03:46.480
Because that's the game.

113
00:03:46.480 --> 00:03:48.880
You start at level zero and then you just level up

114
00:03:48.880 --> 00:03:51.080
your content as you go forward.

115
00:03:51.080 --> 00:03:53.120
The third strategy that is very important

116
00:03:53.120 --> 00:03:55.840
is for you to build your list, your emailing list.

117
00:03:55.840 --> 00:03:58.840
And this is crucial because you need to find a way

118
00:03:58.840 --> 00:04:01.200
to contact these people who are following you

119
00:04:01.200 --> 00:04:02.120
as soon as you can.

120
00:04:02.120 --> 00:04:04.280
Because if you're in the content game for long enough,

121
00:04:04.280 --> 00:04:06.680
you know that if you're constantly posting on TikTok

122
00:04:06.680 --> 00:04:08.040
on YouTube, on Instagram,

123
00:04:08.040 --> 00:04:11.080
your followers there live on rented space.

124
00:04:11.080 --> 00:04:13.560
And what that basically means is that, for example,

125
00:04:13.560 --> 00:04:16.720
if you even unknowingly violate TikTok's content rules,

126
00:04:16.720 --> 00:04:18.800
then if you get like three strikes in that platform,

127
00:04:18.800 --> 00:04:20.600
they can actually permanently ban your account

128
00:04:20.600 --> 00:04:22.160
and all your followers will be removed.

129
00:04:22.160 --> 00:04:25.240
That's why all your followers in those social media platforms

130
00:04:25.240 --> 00:04:26.360
are just being rented.

131
00:04:26.360 --> 00:04:28.080
But if you start to collect an email list,

132
00:04:28.080 --> 00:04:29.200
then that list is yours.

133
00:04:29.200 --> 00:04:30.480
These are people who know you.

134
00:04:30.480 --> 00:04:32.560
These are people that you can reach out to.

135
00:04:32.560 --> 00:04:33.400
And this is very simple.

136
00:04:33.400 --> 00:04:36.200
I've seen people just use like a Google Sheets form,

137
00:04:36.200 --> 00:04:38.880
for example, and use that as a link to drive people to.

138
00:04:38.880 --> 00:04:41.280
But probably one of the easiest and freest ways

139
00:04:41.280 --> 00:04:44.280
that I can recommend to you would be to sign up to Substack.

140
00:04:44.280 --> 00:04:46.720
And that will give you a nice landing page like this

141
00:04:46.720 --> 00:04:48.320
where people can just type their emails

142
00:04:48.320 --> 00:04:49.560
and almost frictionlessly.

143
00:04:49.560 --> 00:04:51.600
You get to capture those emails as you go.

144
00:04:51.600 --> 00:04:54.480
So this literally takes like five minutes to sign up and sign up.

145
00:04:54.480 --> 00:04:56.320
And so as soon as you post your content

146
00:04:56.320 --> 00:04:57.800
and start getting some steam,

147
00:04:57.800 --> 00:05:01.360
I suggest that you have some sort of email capture device in there.

148
00:05:01.360 --> 00:05:03.920
So that slowly but surely you will build a list of people

149
00:05:03.920 --> 00:05:05.480
who actually want to hear from you

150
00:05:05.480 --> 00:05:08.320
and you can contact in the future for your services.

151
00:05:08.320 --> 00:05:10.760
Now there's a question sometimes of how much to post.

152
00:05:10.760 --> 00:05:11.600
Is there a limit?

153
00:05:11.600 --> 00:05:12.640
Can I post three times a day?

154
00:05:12.640 --> 00:05:13.840
Can I post five times a day?

155
00:05:13.840 --> 00:05:16.560
And will that lead me to being banned from these accounts?

156
00:05:16.560 --> 00:05:18.200
Now just to dispel that myth,

157
00:05:18.200 --> 00:05:21.200
in social media platforms, volume is actually key.

158
00:05:21.200 --> 00:05:23.600
So no platform limits how much you can post

159
00:05:23.600 --> 00:05:25.320
as long as you're not classified as a bot.

160
00:05:25.320 --> 00:05:27.960
And I can link the tutorial below on warming up an account

161
00:05:27.960 --> 00:05:29.720
if in case you need to open up a new account.

162
00:05:29.720 --> 00:05:32.440
But generally if you already have like one that you are using,

163
00:05:32.440 --> 00:05:35.680
let's say personally or casually is best to start with that.

164
00:05:35.680 --> 00:05:38.080
And it's also best to start posting organically

165
00:05:38.080 --> 00:05:39.000
from the native apps.

166
00:05:39.000 --> 00:05:40.160
So if you're posting on TikTok,

167
00:05:40.160 --> 00:05:42.960
use the TikTok app to edit and post your videos

168
00:05:42.960 --> 00:05:44.920
instead of going straight to Blotato

169
00:05:44.920 --> 00:05:47.960
or upload posts to automatically post videos for you.

170
00:05:47.960 --> 00:05:49.200
But in terms of the count,

171
00:05:49.200 --> 00:05:52.800
if you can post 10 videos per day organically, then do that.

172
00:05:52.800 --> 00:05:54.840
Now a lot of people probably don't have that bandwidth.

173
00:05:54.840 --> 00:05:57.160
But for example, you go to the RoboNuggets TikTok.

174
00:05:57.160 --> 00:05:59.800
You can see I was posting like two to three times per day here.

175
00:05:59.800 --> 00:06:01.000
And it was pretty easy to do

176
00:06:01.000 --> 00:06:02.920
because I was literally just screen sharing

177
00:06:02.920 --> 00:06:04.640
what I'm seeing and what I was interested in

178
00:06:04.640 --> 00:06:05.640
during that time, right?

179
00:06:05.640 --> 00:06:07.920
And also there is this account called Instant Bollywood

180
00:06:07.920 --> 00:06:11.200
where basically they are posting 100 times per day.

181
00:06:11.200 --> 00:06:13.520
And they get 9.3 billion impressions from that.

182
00:06:13.520 --> 00:06:16.600
And even Instagram commented that this is not a problem at all.

183
00:06:16.600 --> 00:06:18.240
And they can handle the bandwidth of it

184
00:06:18.240 --> 00:06:20.160
because even if they're posting 100 times per day,

185
00:06:20.160 --> 00:06:22.000
honestly, that's like a drop in the ocean

186
00:06:22.000 --> 00:06:23.800
that these platforms can accommodate

187
00:06:23.800 --> 00:06:26.440
because there's millions being posted on these platforms

188
00:06:26.440 --> 00:06:27.720
on a single day probably.

189
00:06:27.720 --> 00:06:30.080
And you can also take a look at the content of Sabrina

190
00:06:30.080 --> 00:06:31.160
who's part of our community

191
00:06:31.160 --> 00:06:33.520
and has been posting on socials for quite a while now.

192
00:06:33.520 --> 00:06:35.240
And she still consistently posts something

193
00:06:35.240 --> 00:06:36.760
like two to three times per day

194
00:06:36.760 --> 00:06:38.320
on these short form platforms.

195
00:06:38.320 --> 00:06:41.080
And what she does is basically batches the content

196
00:06:41.080 --> 00:06:43.200
she produces on Saturdays, let's say.

197
00:06:43.200 --> 00:06:44.480
And that would be her content day

198
00:06:44.480 --> 00:06:46.400
where she schedules everything by batch.

199
00:06:46.400 --> 00:06:49.920
But the point being that more content equals more chances

200
00:06:49.920 --> 00:06:50.760
to be discovered.

201
00:06:50.760 --> 00:06:52.040
So do not hold back.

202
00:06:52.040 --> 00:06:53.640
And there's multiple approaches on this,

203
00:06:53.640 --> 00:06:55.800
but if you need like a formula or a framework,

204
00:06:55.800 --> 00:06:58.760
you can use this where you can post two to three times per day

205
00:06:58.760 --> 00:06:59.640
as an intention.

206
00:06:59.640 --> 00:07:01.360
You can just set up like one day in the week

207
00:07:01.360 --> 00:07:02.600
where you batch things

208
00:07:02.600 --> 00:07:04.720
and you probably don't need to do 100 per day,

209
00:07:04.720 --> 00:07:07.320
but just keep that in mind that there are some creators

210
00:07:07.320 --> 00:07:08.640
who are pushing this to the limit

211
00:07:08.640 --> 00:07:10.880
and still finding a lot of success on it.

212
00:07:10.880 --> 00:07:12.000
And so that's the formula.

213
00:07:12.000 --> 00:07:13.200
You need to have great hooks,

214
00:07:13.200 --> 00:07:14.880
you need to have consistency in volume

215
00:07:14.880 --> 00:07:17.360
and you need to always have that value exchange.

216
00:07:17.360 --> 00:07:19.400
So you need to make your content selfless

217
00:07:19.400 --> 00:07:20.400
instead of selfish.

218
00:07:20.400 --> 00:07:22.240
And what that means is basically just thinking

219
00:07:22.240 --> 00:07:24.880
about the person watching on the other side of the screen

220
00:07:24.880 --> 00:07:26.920
and talking about how this specific thing

221
00:07:26.920 --> 00:07:29.360
that you're sharing would be valuable for them.

222
00:07:29.360 --> 00:07:30.600
And honestly, just to start,

223
00:07:30.600 --> 00:07:33.280
you'll get better as you go and the key is to just begin

224
00:07:33.280 --> 00:07:34.640
because every simple post,

225
00:07:34.640 --> 00:07:35.960
no matter how unpolished that is,

226
00:07:35.960 --> 00:07:37.280
that will teach you something.

227
00:07:37.280 --> 00:07:39.480
And so my challenge to you is after watching

228
00:07:39.480 --> 00:07:40.640
this specific video,

229
00:07:40.640 --> 00:07:42.680
I want you to actually start recording something,

230
00:07:42.680 --> 00:07:44.840
talk about a topic that you learned about,

231
00:07:44.840 --> 00:07:47.800
let's say AI today, point your phone into your screen

232
00:07:47.800 --> 00:07:50.120
and post something on TikTok or Instagram.

233
00:07:50.120 --> 00:07:52.640
Now, next up, let's talk about productizing your offer

234
00:07:52.640 --> 00:07:55.080
so that we can make it as easy as possible to sell.
